window.QDATA_2 = [{"id":"af8","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2026 1H Q18","q":"Simplify fully (4x^2-9)/(2x^2-5x-12). Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(2x-3)/(x-4)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Numerator: 4x²-9 = (2x-3)(2x+3) (difference of squares)","Denominator: 2x²-5x-12 = (2x+3)(x-4)","Cancel the common factor (2x+3): (2x-3)/(x-4)"]},{"id":"af9","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Nov 2024 2H Q12","q":"(a) Solve (3x+2)/5 - (2x+1)/3 = x. Show clear algebraic working. (b) Make c the subject of the formula f = sqrt((a+bc)/(c-d))","answer":"(a) x = 1/16 (b) c = (a+f²d)/(f²-b)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Multiply by 15: 3(3x+2) - 5(2x+1) = 15x → 9x+6-10x-5=15x → -x+1=15x → 1=16x → x=1/16","(b) Square both sides: f² = (a+bc)/(c-d) → f²(c-d)=a+bc → f²c-f²d=a+bc → f²c-bc=a+f²d → c(f²-b)=a+f²d → c=(a+f²d)/(f²-b)"]},{"id":"af10","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2024 1H Q12","q":"(a) Factorise fully 6y^2-5y-4. (b) Express (2x+1)/(4x) + (7-5x)/(3x) as a single fraction in its simplest form.","answer":"(a) (3y-4)(2y+1) (b) (31-14x)/(12x)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 6y²-5y-4 = (3y-4)(2y+1), check: 6y²+3y-8y-4=6y²-5y-4 ✓","(b) Common denominator 12x: (2x+1)/4x=(6x+3)/12x and (7-5x)/3x=(28-20x)/12x","Add: (6x+3+28-20x)/12x = (31-14x)/(12x)"]},{"id":"af11","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2024 2H Q20","q":"Given that k = x-y and x = 1/(4y), express 5k/(x+2) in the form (a-by^2)/(c+dy) where a, b, c and d are integers.","answer":"(5-20y²)/(1+8y), so a=5, b=20, c=1, d=8","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["k = x-y = 1/(4y) - y = (1-4y²)/(4y)","5k = (5-20y²)/(4y)","x+2 = 1/(4y)+2 = (1+8y)/(4y)","5k/(x+2) = [(5-20y²)/(4y)] ÷ [(1+8y)/(4y)] = (5-20y²)/(1+8y)"]},{"id":"af12","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Jan 2023 2H Q13","q":"Solve (x+3)/4 - (7-x)/5 = 4.3. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 11","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply by 20: 5(x+3) - 4(7-x) = 86","5x+15-28+4x=86 → 9x-13=86 → 9x=99 → x=11"]},{"id":"af13","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2022 1H Q11","q":"(a) Factorise 9x^2-4y^2. (b) Express 7/8 - (x+3)/(4x) as a single fraction in its simplest form.","answer":"(a) (3x-2y)(3x+2y) (b) (5x-6)/(8x)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Difference of squares: 9x²-4y²=(3x)²-(2y)²=(3x-2y)(3x+2y)","(b) Common denominator 8x: 7/8=7x/8x and (x+3)/4x=(2x+6)/8x","Subtract: (7x-2x-6)/8x = (5x-6)/(8x)"]},{"id":"af14","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q23","q":"Given a = (2x+5)/(1-x) and x = (5-2y)/(3y), write a in the form (m+ny)/(p(y-1)) where m, n and p are integers. Show your working clearly.","answer":"(11y+10)/(5(y-1)), so m=10, n=11, p=5","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["1-x = 1 - (5-2y)/(3y) = (3y-5+2y)/(3y) = (5y-5)/(3y) = 5(y-1)/(3y)","2x+5 = (10-4y)/(3y) + 15y/(3y) = (10+11y)/(3y)","a = [(10+11y)/(3y)] ÷ [5(y-1)/(3y)] = (10+11y)/(5(y-1)) = (11y+10)/(5(y-1))"]},{"id":"af15","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2025 2H Q23","q":"(4x^2-4x-120)/(5x^2-180) ÷ (x^2+5x)/(10x^2+60x) = p where p is an integer. Find the value of p. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"p = 8","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["4x²-4x-120 = 4(x²-x-30) = 4(x-6)(x+5)","5x²-180 = 5(x²-36) = 5(x-6)(x+6)","x²+5x = x(x+5); 10x²+60x = 10x(x+6)","Dividing by a fraction means multiplying by its reciprocal: [4(x-6)(x+5)/(5(x-6)(x+6))] × [10x(x+6)/(x(x+5))]","Cancel (x-6), (x+5), (x+6), x: 4×10/5 = 8"]},{"id":"af16","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Nov 2024 2H Q23","q":"Show that (16x^2-36)/(x-7) ÷ (2x^2+7x+6)/(x^2-5x-14) - (7+8x) = n where n is an integer to be found. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"n = -19","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["16x²-36 = 4(4x²-9) = 4(2x-3)(2x+3)","2x²+7x+6 = (2x+3)(x+2); x²-5x-14 = (x-7)(x+2)","Division: [4(2x-3)(2x+3)/(x-7)] × [(x-7)(x+2)/((2x+3)(x+2))] = 4(2x-3), after cancelling (x-7), (2x+3), (x+2)","4(2x-3) = 8x-12, so the expression is 8x-12-(7+8x) = 8x-12-7-8x = -19"]},{"id":"af17","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2024 2H Q14","q":"(a) Show that 3y(2y+5)(y+7) can be written in the form ay^3+by^2+cy where a, b and c are integers. (b) Solve (2x+3)/5 + (6x-5)/4 = 163/100. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a) 6y³+57y²+105y, so a=6, b=57, c=105 (b) x = 1.2","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (2y+5)(y+7) = 2y²+14y+5y+35 = 2y²+19y+35; then 3y(2y²+19y+35) = 6y³+57y²+105y","(b) Multiply by 20: 4(2x+3)+5(6x-5) = 20×1.63 = 32.6","8x+12+30x-25=32.6 → 38x-13=32.6 → 38x=45.6 → x=1.2"]},{"id":"af18","topic":"algfrac","ref":"Nov 2023 2H Q24","q":"Solve (45x^3-80x)/(3x^2+x-4) × (1/(3x-4) + 1/x) = 4(x+2)/(5x-8). Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 1.75","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["45x³-80x = 5x(9x²-16) = 5x(3x-4)(3x+4); 3x²+x-4 = (3x+4)(x-1)","First fraction simplifies: 5x(3x-4)(3x+4)/[(3x+4)(x-1)] = 5x(3x-4)/(x-1)","1/(3x-4) + 1/x = [x+(3x-4)]/[x(3x-4)] = (4x-4)/[x(3x-4)] = 4(x-1)/[x(3x-4)]","Multiply: [5x(3x-4)/(x-1)] × [4(x-1)/(x(3x-4))] = 20 (everything cancels)","So 20 = 4(x+2)/(5x-8) → 20(5x-8)=4(x+2) → 100x-160=4x+8 → 96x=168 → x=1.75"]},{"id":"af19","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2022 2H Q15","q":"(a) Solve (4x+5)/3 - (3-2x)/2 = 13. Show clear algebraic working. (b) Solve the inequality 2y^2-7y-30 ≤ 0. Show your working clearly.","answer":"(a) x = 5.5 (b) -2.5 ≤ y ≤ 6","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Multiply by 6: 2(4x+5) - 3(3-2x) = 78 → 8x+10-9+6x=78 → 14x+1=78 → 14x=77 → x=5.5","(b) Factorise 2y²-7y-30 = (2y+5)(y-6), roots y=-2.5 and y=6","Parabola opens upward, so ≤0 between the roots: -2.5 ≤ y ≤ 6"]},{"id":"af20","topic":"algfrac","ref":"June 2022 2H Q19","q":"Given that a = 14/(3x-7) and x = 7/(4y-3), express a in the form (py+q)/(ry+s) where p, q, r and s are integers. Give your answer in its simplest form.","answer":"(4y-3)/(3-2y), so p=4, q=-3, r=-2, s=3","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3x-7 = 21/(4y-3) - 7 = [21-7(4y-3)]/(4y-3) = (42-28y)/(4y-3)","a = 14 ÷ [(42-28y)/(4y-3)] = 14(4y-3)/(42-28y)","42-28y = 14(3-2y), so a = 14(4y-3)/[14(3-2y)] = (4y-3)/(3-2y)"]},{"id":"eq1","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 1F Q5","q":"(a) Simplify d+d+d+d+d. (b) Simplify 3m-m+8m. (c) Simplify 6×3y. (d) Solve 15-a=9","answer":"(a) 5d (b) 10m (c) 18y (d) a=6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq2","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 2F Q12","q":"Hugo sells x bags of potatoes (6 each) and y sacks of potatoes (20 each). The total number of potatoes Hugo sells is T. Write down a formula for T in terms of x and y.","answer":"T = 6x+20y","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq3","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q4","q":"(a) Simplify y+y+y+y+y. (b) Simplify c×c×c×c. (c) Solve 4x=48. (d) Solve 18-w=13","answer":"(a) 5y (b) c^4 (c) x=12 (d) w=5","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq4","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q6","q":"Here is a number machine: input → ×3 → -9 → output. (a) Find the output when the input is 8. A different number machine: input → +12 → [box] → output. When the input is 8 the output is 4. (b) Complete the box to give a possible number machine.","answer":"(a) 15 (b) subtract 16 (input 8 → +12 = 20 → -16 = 4)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 8×3=24, 24-9=15","(b) 8+12=20, and the output is 4, so the box must subtract 16"]},{"id":"eq5","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q8","q":"T=5n-3p. (a) Work out the value of T when n=8 and p=4.5. (b) Solve 5h+8=30","answer":"(a) T=26.5 (b) h=4.4","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) T=5(8)-3(4.5)=40-13.5=26.5","(b) 5h+8=30 → 5h=22 → h=4.4"]},{"id":"eq6","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 1F Q4","q":"(a) Simplify 4×5e. (b) Solve f+14=29","answer":"(a) 20e (b) f=15","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq7","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 2F Q3","q":"(a) Simplify d+d+d+d. (b) Simplify w×w×w×w×w. (c) Solve 6x=42. (d) Simplify 7r+9y+3r-4y","answer":"(a) 4d (b) w^5 (c) x=7 (d) 10r+5y","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq8","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q5","q":"(a) Simplify 8d-4d+7d. (b) Simplify m×10p. (c) Solve x+5=-19. (d) Solve y/8=6. (e) Simplify a×a×a×a. k=8 and n=12. (f) Work out the value of 9k-4n","answer":"(a) 11d (b) 10mp (c) x=-24 (d) y=48 (e) a^4 (f) 24","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(f) 9(8)-4(12)=72-48=24"]},{"id":"eq9","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q11","q":"Make d the subject of the formula c=8d+5","answer":"d = (c-5)/8","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq10","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 1F Q2","q":"(a) Simplify 10p-4p+9p. (b) Simplify 9×4q. (c) Solve 4r=15","answer":"(a) 15p (b) 36q (c) r=3.75","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq11","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 1F Q8","q":"(a) Simplify 10x-7y-6x+4y. T=4d-6e. (b) Work out the value of T when d=13 and e=7. (c) Solve 5p+11=28","answer":"(a) 4x-3y (b) T=10 (c) p=3.4","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) T=4(13)-6(7)=52-42=10","(c) 5p+11=28 → 5p=17 → p=3.4"]},{"id":"eq12","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q7","q":"(a) Simplify 9d×5c. (b) Simplify 7p+5n-9p+3n. T=8e-6f. (c) Work out the value of T when e=9 and f=5. (d) Solve 5m-6=17","answer":"(a) 45cd (b) -2p+8n (c) T=42 (d) m=4.6","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) T=8(9)-6(5)=72-30=42","(d) 5m-6=17 → 5m=23 → m=4.6"]},{"id":"eq13","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q10","q":"A number machine: input → ×y → -17 → output. When the input is 7 the output is 60. (a) Work out the value of y. A different number machine: input → +7 → ÷5 → output. The input is x. (b) Write down an expression, in terms of x, for the output.","answer":"(a) y=11 (b) (x+7)/5","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 7y-17=60 → 7y=77 → y=11"]},{"id":"eq14","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2023 1F Q5","q":"(a) Simplify p+p+p+p. (b) Simplify 5e+6f+7e-2f. (c) Solve 13-x=7. (d) Solve 4y+7=43","answer":"(a) 4p (b) 12e+4f (c) x=6 (d) y=9","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq15","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2023 1F Q9","q":"A number machine: input → ×10 → +6 → output. (a) Work out the output when the input is 14. A different number machine: input → [box] → +9 → output. When the input is 11 the output is 64. (b) Write a number on the dotted line to complete the number machine.","answer":"(a) 146 (b) ×5 (11×5=55, 55+9=64)","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 14×10+6=146","(b) output before +9 is 64-9=55; 55÷11=5, so the box multiplies by 5"]},{"id":"eq16","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q7","q":"(a) Simplify 5p×9k. (b) Simplify 3e+2f+8e-7f. (c) Solve 2d+7=16","answer":"(a) 45pk (b) 11e-5f (c) d=4.5","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq17","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q13","q":"p=t-ac where t=18, a=-3, c=5. (a) Work out the value of p. (b) Make x the subject of the formula d=3x+10","answer":"(a) p=33 (b) x=(d-10)/3","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) p=18-(-3)(5)=18+15=33"]},{"id":"eq18","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q8","q":"A number machine: input → ×5 → -7 → output. (a) Work out the output when the input is 9. A different number machine: input → ÷5 → [box] → output. When the input is 30 the output is 18. (b) Find a suitable way to complete the number machine. The rule: Total cost = 8 euros per day plus 5 euros. James hires a cement mixer for 3 days. (c) Work out the cost to James. The cost to Sophia is 61 euros. (d) For how many days does Sophia hire the cement mixer?","answer":"(a) 38 (b) ×3 (c) 29 euros (d) 7 days","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 9×5-7=38","(b) 30÷5=6, and 6→18 so box multiplies by 3","(c) 8(3)+5=29","(d) 61=8d+5 → 8d=56 → d=7"]},{"id":"eq19","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 1F Q2","q":"(a) Simplify 12a+3a-7a. (b) Simplify 8×3b. (c) Solve c/3=9","answer":"(a) 8a (b) 24b (c) c=27","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq20","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 1F Q8","q":"(a) Simplify 12g-8e-5g+6e. A=3b-5c. (b) Work out the value of A when b=12 and c=4. (c) Solve 4p+9=24","answer":"(a) 7g-2e (b) A=16 (c) p=3.75","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) A=3(12)-5(4)=36-20=16","(c) 4p+9=24 → 4p=15 → p=3.75"]},{"id":"eq21","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q7","q":"(a) Solve 5x=30. (b) Solve y-7=12. (c) Simplify h+h+h+h+h. (d) Simplify 5a+7f-2a+4f","answer":"(a) x=6 (b) y=19 (c) 5h (d) 3a+11f","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq22","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 1F Q27","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 4x+3y=9 and 2x-2y=-13. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = -1.5, y = 5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply first eqn by 2: 8x+6y=18. Multiply second by 3: 6x-6y=-39","Add: 14x=-21 → x=-1.5","Substitute into 2x-2y=-13: -3-2y=-13 → y=5"]},{"id":"eq23","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 2F Q9","q":"(a) Simplify 5h+6p+2h-9p. (b) Work out the value of 4c-3r when c=9 and r=5. (c) Solve 4n-9=21","answer":"(a) 7h-3p (b) 21 (c) n=7.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 4(9)-3(5)=36-15=21","(c) 4n-9=21 → 4n=30 → n=7.5"]},{"id":"eq24","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q12","q":"(a) Find the value of d^2-3 when d=-5. (b) Make r the subject of the formula m=4r-h. Rachel is an electrician: amount charged = multiply hours worked by 27, then add 40. Rachel works n hours and charges £P. (c) Write down a formula for P in terms of n.","answer":"(a) 22 (b) r=(m+h)/4 (c) P=27n+40","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) (-5)²-3=25-3=22"]},{"id":"eq25","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q19","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 5x+y=11 and 3x-y=9. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 2.5, y = -1.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Add the two equations: 8x=20 → x=2.5","Substitute into 5x+y=11: 12.5+y=11 → y=-1.5"]},{"id":"eq26","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 1F Q14","q":"(a) Expand x(x-7). (b) Factorise 8y-10. m=5a+7b. (c) Work out the value of a when m=48 and b=3","answer":"(a) x²-7x (b) 2(4y-5) (c) a=5.4","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) 48=5a+7(3)=5a+21 → 5a=27 → a=5.4"]},{"id":"eq27","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 1F Q23","q":"(a) Solve x-4=(3+2x)/6. Show clear algebraic working. (b)(i) Factorise y^2-11y+30. (ii) Hence solve y^2-11y+30=0","answer":"(a) x=6.75 (b)(i) (y-5)(y-6) (ii) y=5 or y=6","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Multiply by 6: 6x-24=3+2x → 4x=27 → x=6.75"]},{"id":"eq28","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 2F Q10","q":"Lui works out 30-4x when x=-5 as: 30-4×-5 = 30-20 = 10. Lui's answer is wrong. (a) Explain what Lui has done wrong. Oni thinks of a positive, odd number Y with Y≤9. (b) Write down all the possible values of Y.","answer":"(a) Lui treated -4×-5 as -20 instead of +20 (he did not correctly multiply the two negatives, which should give a positive 20, so the answer should be 30+20=50) (b) Y = 1, 3, 5, 7, 9","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq29","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 2F Q12","q":"(a) Make y the subject of w=3y-d. Diego buys b boxes (12 crayons each) and p packets (3 crayons each) of crayons, a total of T crayons. (b) Write down a formula for T in terms of b and p.","answer":"(a) y=(w+d)/3 (b) T=12b+3p","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"eq30","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 2F Q25","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 3x+5y=8 and 4x+y=-3.5. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = -1.5, y = 2.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["From the second equation: y=-3.5-4x","Substitute: 3x+5(-3.5-4x)=8 → 3x-17.5-20x=8 → -17x=25.5 → x=-1.5","y=-3.5-4(-1.5)=2.5"]},{"id":"eq31","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q20","q":"(a) Simplify (p^3)^5. (b) Expand and simplify 2n(4n+3)+n(n-4). (c) Solve (2x+5)/3=4-x. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a) p^15 (b) 9n²+2n (c) x=1.4","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 2n(4n+3)=8n²+6n; n(n-4)=n²-4n; sum=9n²+2n","(c) Multiply by 3: 2x+5=12-3x → 5x=7 → x=1.4"]},{"id":"eq32","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 2F Q26","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 6x+4y=1 and 3x+5y=8. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = -1.5, y = 2.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply the second equation by 2: 6x+10y=16","Subtract the first equation: 6y=15 → y=2.5","Substitute into 3x+5y=8: 3x+12.5=8 → x=-1.5"]},{"id":"eq33","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2023 1F Q8","q":"Carla wraps 2 large parcels (185 cm of ribbon each) and 3 small parcels (p cm of ribbon each). In total she uses exactly 7 metres of ribbon. Find the value of p.","answer":"p = 110","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["2(185)+3p=700 → 370+3p=700 → 3p=330 → p=110"]},{"id":"eq34","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2023 1F Q24","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 2x+9y=14.5 and 7x+3y=8. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 0.5, y = 1.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply the second equation by 3: 21x+9y=24","Subtract the first equation: 19x=9.5 → x=0.5","Substitute into 7x+3y=8: 3.5+3y=8 → y=1.5"]},{"id":"eq35","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q17","q":"Solve 3(2-4x)=5-8x. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 0.25","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["6-12x=5-8x","1=4x, so x=0.25"]},{"id":"eq36","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q22","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 5x+4y=-2 and 2x-y=4.4. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 1.2, y = -2","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["From the second equation: y=2x-4.4","Substitute: 5x+4(2x-4.4)=-2 → 5x+8x-17.6=-2 → 13x=15.6 → x=1.2","y=2(1.2)-4.4=-2"]},{"id":"eq37","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q17","q":"Molly uses this number machine to work out the tax to pay on her earnings: number of hours worked → multiply by 12 → add 50 → multiply by 0.2 → amount of tax £T. When Molly works n hours the tax is £T. Find a formula for T in terms of n.","answer":"T = 2.4n + 10","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["T=0.2(12n+50) = 2.4n+10"]},{"id":"eq38","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q24","q":"2^k / 4^n = 2^x. Find an expression for x in terms of k and n.","answer":"x = k - 2n","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["4^n = (2²)^n = 2^(2n)","2^k / 2^(2n) = 2^(k-2n) = 2^x, so x=k-2n"]},{"id":"eq39","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q26","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 7x+3y=3 and 3x-y=7. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 1.5, y = -2.5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["From the second equation: y=3x-7","Substitute: 7x+3(3x-7)=3 → 7x+9x-21=3 → 16x=24 → x=1.5","y=3(1.5)-7=-2.5"]},{"id":"eq40","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q12","q":"Alisa, Jena and Mikael each pick cucumbers. Alisa picks C cucumbers. Jena picks 5 fewer than Alisa. Mikael picks twice as many as Alisa. The total is T. Find a formula for T in terms of C, in its simplest form.","answer":"T = 4C - 5","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["T = C + (C-5) + 2C = 4C-5"]},{"id":"eq41","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q8","q":"Danielle prints business cards: Total cost = price per card × number of cards + fixed fee, where price per card = 0.14 euros and fixed fee = 25 euros. She prints 350 cards. Work out the total cost.","answer":"74 euros","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["0.14×350+25 = 49+25 = 74"]},{"id":"eq42","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q15","q":"(a) Solve 5c=15. (b) Expand x(8-x). T=5m-6n. (c) Work out the value of T when m=4.2 and n=-2.5. (d) Make g the subject of k=2g+t","answer":"(a) c=3 (b) 8x-x² (c) T=36 (d) g=(k-t)/2","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(c) T=5(4.2)-6(-2.5)=21+15=36"]},{"id":"eq43","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q25","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 3x+5y=3.1 and 6x+3y=3.75. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 0.45, y = 0.35","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply the first equation by 2: 6x+10y=6.2","Subtract the second equation: 7y=2.45 → y=0.35","Substitute into 3x+5y=3.1: 3x+1.75=3.1 → x=0.45"]},{"id":"eq44","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q15","q":"Sid has n counters. Erin has 7 more counters than Sid. Kabir has 3 times as many as Sid. (a) Write down an expression, in terms of n, for the total number of counters Sid, Erin and Kabir have. Kabir has 72 counters. (b) How many counters does Erin have?","answer":"(a) 5n+7 (b) 31","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) n+(n+7)+3n = 5n+7","(b) 3n=72 → n=24; Erin=n+7=31"]},{"id":"eq45","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 2F Q7","q":"2 jugs each contain 350 millilitres of milk. 5 bottles each contain y millilitres of milk. Peter tips all the milk from the 2 jugs and 5 bottles into a container. The total is 2.8 litres. Work out the value of y.","answer":"y = 420","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["2(350)+5y=2800 → 700+5y=2800 → 5y=2100 → y=420"]},{"id":"eq46","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q16","q":"(a) Factorise fully 12pq-18p. There are 56 metal bars in a box, each gold, silver or zinc. y bars are gold, (3y+7) are silver, (2y-5) are zinc. (b) Work out the number of metal bars that are zinc. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(a) 6p(2q-3) (b) 13","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) y+(3y+7)+(2y-5)=56 → 6y+2=56 → 6y=54 → y=9; zinc=2(9)-5=13"]},{"id":"eq47","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q20","q":"(a) Solve (2x+5)/6 = 2x-5. Show clear algebraic working. (b) Simplify h^15 ÷ h^3. (c) Simplify fully (2g^3k^5)^4. (d) Given that (y^5 × y^n)/y^7 = y^12, work out the value of n.","answer":"(a) x=3.5 (b) h^12 (c) 16g^12k^20 (d) n=14","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Multiply by 6: 2x+5=12x-30 → 35=10x → x=3.5","(d) y^(5+n-7)=y^(n-2)=y^12, so n-2=12 → n=14"]},{"id":"eq48","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2022 2F Q9","q":"3 cups each contain 200 millilitres of water. 4 jugs each contain x millilitres of water. Emma pours all the water from the 3 cups and 4 jugs into a container. The total is 3.5 litres. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 725","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3(200)+4x=3500 → 600+4x=3500 → 4x=2900 → x=725"]},{"id":"eq49","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 2H Q18","q":"Make x the subject of the formula a = (3w-x^2)/(x^2+6)","answer":"x = sqrt[(3w-6a)/(a+1)]","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["a(x²+6)=3w-x²","ax²+6a=3w-x²","x²(a+1)=3w-6a","x²=(3w-6a)/(a+1), so x=√[(3w-6a)/(a+1)]"]},{"id":"eq50","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q18","q":"Make y the subject of p = sqrt[(y+w)/(3y-t)]","answer":"y = (w+p²t)/(3p²-1)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["p²=(y+w)/(3y-t)","p²(3y-t)=y+w","3p²y-p²t=y+w","y(3p²-1)=w+p²t, so y=(w+p²t)/(3p²-1)"]},{"id":"eq51","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 2H Q16","q":"Make t the subject of the formula c = (t^2+3)/(7-8t^2)","answer":"t = sqrt[(7c-3)/(1+8c)]","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["c(7-8t²)=t²+3","7c-8ct²=t²+3","7c-3=t²(1+8c)","t²=(7c-3)/(1+8c), so t=√[(7c-3)/(1+8c)]"]},{"id":"eq52","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2023 1H Q15","q":"Make n the subject of the formula x = (3p+n)/(3n-4)","answer":"n = (3p+4x)/(3x-1)","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["x(3n-4)=3p+n","3xn-4x=3p+n","n(3x-1)=3p+4x, so n=(3p+4x)/(3x-1)"]},{"id":"eq53","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 1H Q23","q":"A bag contains x marbles, 12 of which are pink and the rest yellow. Greta takes at random 2 marbles. The probability she takes a pink marble and a yellow marble is 18/47. Work out the value of x. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"x = 48","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["P = 2 × (12/x) × ((x-12)/(x-1)) = 18/47","24(x-12) × 47 = 18x(x-1)","1128x-13536 = 18x²-18x","18x²-1146x+13536=0, divide by 6: 3x²-191x+2256=0","Discriminant = 191²-4(3)(2256) = 36481-27072 = 9409 = 97²","x = (191±97)/6 = 48 or 94/6 (not an integer) — so x=48"]},{"id":"eq54","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2026 2H Q23","q":"The straight line L has equation y=3x-2. The curve C has equation x^2+y^2-2y=12. Find the coordinates of the points where L and C intersect. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(2, 4) and (-0.2, -2.6)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Substitute y=3x-2: x²+(3x-2)²-2(3x-2)=12","x²+9x²-12x+4-6x+4=12 → 10x²-18x+8=12 → 10x²-18x-4=0","Divide by 2: 5x²-9x-2=0 → (5x+1)(x-2)=0 → x=2 or x=-0.2","x=2: y=4. x=-0.2: y=-2.6"]},{"id":"eq55","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 1H Q28","q":"The curve C has equation x^2+y^2=d-11x where d is an integer. The line L has equation y=3x+e where e is an integer. C and L intersect at points A and B. The coordinates of A are (0.2, 2.6). Work out the coordinates of B. Show your working clearly.","answer":"B = (-2.5, -5.5)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Substitute A into L: 2.6=3(0.2)+e → e=2","Substitute A into C: 0.2²+2.6²=d-11(0.2) → 6.8=d-2.2 → d=9","So C: x²+11x+y²=9, and L: y=3x+2","Substitute: x²+11x+(3x+2)²=9 → 10x²+23x+4=9 → 10x²+23x-5=0","x=0.2 is one root (point A); sum of roots=-2.3, so the other root is x=-2.5","y=3(-2.5)+2=-5.5"]},{"id":"eq56","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2025 2H Q20","q":"A quadratic equation ax^2+4x+c=0 has solutions x=(-4±2√39)/10. Find the value of a and the value of c. Show your working clearly.","answer":"a = 5, c = -7","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["By the quadratic formula, x=(-4±√(16-4ac))/(2a)","Comparing denominators: 2a=10, so a=5","Comparing the surd: 16-4ac=4×39=156 → -4ac=140 → ac=-35 → c=-35/5=-7"]},{"id":"eq57","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2025 1H Q22","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations x^2+3y+y^2=7 and y=x+2. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(-0.5, 1.5) and (-3, -1)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Substitute y=x+2: x²+3(x+2)+(x+2)²=7","x²+3x+6+x²+4x+4=7 → 2x²+7x+10=7 → 2x²+7x+3=0","(2x+1)(x+3)=0 → x=-0.5 or x=-3","x=-0.5: y=1.5. x=-3: y=-1"]},{"id":"eq58","topic":"equations","ref":"Nov 2024 2H Q22","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations x^2+y^2+y=3 and x+2=y. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(-1.5, 0.5) and (-1, 1)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["From the second equation: x=y-2","Substitute: (y-2)²+y²+y=3 → y²-4y+4+y²+y=3 → 2y²-3y+1=0","(2y-1)(y-1)=0 → y=0.5 or y=1","y=0.5: x=-1.5. y=1: x=-1"]},{"id":"eq59","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 2H Q15","q":"(a) Make g the subject of e=sqrt[(7g+5)/(11+2g)]. (b) Solve the inequality 3y^2+4y-32>0. Show your working clearly.","answer":"(a) g=(5-11e²)/(2e²-7) (b) y<-4 or y>8/3","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) e²(11+2g)=7g+5 → 11e²+2e²g=7g+5 → g(2e²-7)=5-11e² → g=(5-11e²)/(2e²-7)","(b) Factorise: 3y²+4y-32=(3y-8)(y+4), roots y=8/3 and y=-4; parabola opens upward so expression is positive outside the roots"]},{"id":"eq60","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2024 2H Q22","q":"The straight line L has equation x+y=5. The curve C has equation 2x^2+3y^2=210. Find the coordinates of the points where L and C intersect. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(9, -4) and (-3, 8)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["From L: y=5-x. Substitute: 2x²+3(5-x)²=210","2x²+75-30x+3x²=210 → 5x²-30x-135=0","Divide by 5: x²-6x-27=0 → (x-9)(x+3)=0 → x=9 or x=-3","x=9: y=-4. x=-3: y=8"]},{"id":"eq62","topic":"equations","ref":"June 2023 2H Q21","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 2x^2+3y^2=11 and x=3y-1. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(2, 1) and (-16/7, -3/7)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Substitute x=3y-1: 2(3y-1)²+3y²=11","2(9y²-6y+1)+3y²=11 → 18y²-12y+2+3y²=11 → 21y²-12y-9=0","Divide by 3: 7y²-4y-3=0 → (7y+3)(y-1)=0 → y=1 or y=-3/7","y=1: x=2. y=-3/7: x=3(-3/7)-1=-16/7"]},{"id":"eq63","topic":"equations","ref":"Jan 2022 1H Q19","q":"Solve the simultaneous equations 3x^2+y^2-xy=5 and y=2x-3. Show clear algebraic working.","answer":"(1, -1) and (0.8, -1.4)","level":"challenge","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Substitute y=2x-3: 3x²+(2x-3)²-x(2x-3)=5","3x²+4x²-12x+9-2x²+3x=5 → 5x²-9x+9=5 → 5x²-9x+4=0","(5x-4)(x-1)=0 → x=1 or x=0.8","x=1: y=-1. x=0.8: y=-1.4"]},{"id":"un1","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 2F Q3","q":"(a) Write down a suitable metric unit for the weight of an apple. Here are four quadrilaterals A, B, C, D (shown in the image); one of them is a rhombus. (b) Write down the letter of the quadrilateral that is a rhombus.","answer":"(a) grams (b) B","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un2","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q6","q":"Paulo has flour in three containers: A=500 grams, B=1 kilogram, C=700 grams. The total weight of Paulo's flour is less than 3 kilograms. How much less? Give your answer in grams.","answer":"800 grams","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Total = 500+1000+700 = 2200 g = 2.2 kg","3 kg - 2.2 kg = 0.8 kg = 800 g"]},{"id":"un3","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2025 1F Q7","q":"Betty got on a plane at 0910. She got off the plane at 1345 the same day. For how long was Betty on the plane? Give your answer in hours and minutes.","answer":"4 hours 35 minutes","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un4","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q7","q":"Tara buys two magazines for 3.25 dirhams each, one bag of sweets for 2.60 dirhams, and three bars of chocolate for 1.75 dirhams each. Tara pays with a 20 dirham note. How much change should she get?","answer":"5.65 dirhams","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["2(3.25)+2.60+3(1.75) = 6.50+2.60+5.25 = 14.35","20-14.35 = 5.65"]},{"id":"un5","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q14","q":"A car travels for 3 hours at an average speed of 78 km/h. Work out the total distance the car travels.","answer":"234 km","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["distance = speed × time = 78×3 = 234 km"]},{"id":"un6","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q6","q":"Plates cost $14 each. Ben has $250 to spend. Ben buys as many plates as he can. How much of the $250 does he have left?","answer":"$12","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["250÷14 = 17.86, so Ben buys 17 plates","17×14 = 238; 250-238 = 12"]},{"id":"un7","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q9","q":"Don got on a bus at 0735. He got off the bus at 1325. How long was Don on the bus? Give your answer in hours and minutes.","answer":"5 hours 50 minutes","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un8","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q4","q":"Barney went for 4 walks on Tuesday, of lengths 800 metres, 2 kilometres, 1.7 kilometres, and x metres. The total length of the 4 walks was 6250 metres. Work out the value of x.","answer":"x = 1750","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["800+2000+1700+x = 6250 → 4500+x=6250 → x=1750"]},{"id":"un9","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 1F Q4","q":"(a) Write 4.15 pm as a time using the 24-hour clock. On Thursday, Belina drives to Theo's house. She leaves home at 0915 and arrives at 1440. (b) Work out how long the journey takes. Give your answer in hours and minutes.","answer":"(a) 16:15 (b) 5 hours 25 minutes","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un10","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 2F Q14","q":"1 dollar = 0.85 euros, 1 dollar = 6.45 yuan. (a) Change 720 dollars to euros. (b) Change 2580 yuan to euros.","answer":"(a) 612 euros (b) 340 euros","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 720×0.85=612","(b) 2580÷6.45=400 dollars; 400×0.85=340 euros"]},{"id":"un11","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q6","q":"(a) Write 5:15 pm using the 24-hour clock. Roberta goes out for a walk. She leaves home at 1635 and arrives back home at 2015 the same day. (b) Work out for how much time Roberta is out for her walk.","answer":"(a) 17:15 (b) 3 hours 40 minutes","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un12","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q5","q":"Brigid recorded the distance she ran on three days: Monday 5950 m, Tuesday 14.5 km, Wednesday 9000 m. Brigid set herself the target of running a total of at least 30 km on these three days. Show that Brigid did not achieve her target.","answer":"Total = 5950+14500+9000 = 29450 m = 29.45 km, which is less than 30 km (0.55 km short), so she did not achieve her target.","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"},{"id":"un13","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q8","q":"Jordan buys 256 notebooks. He buys them in packs of 8, with each pack of 8 costing £2.48. Work out how much the 256 notebooks cost Jordan.","answer":"£79.36","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["256÷8=32 packs","32×2.48 = 79.36"]},{"id":"un14","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q8","q":"Mairi has a 2 metre length of string. She cuts from the string as many lengths of 35 centimetres as possible. Work out the length of string that she has left. Give your answer in centimetres.","answer":"25 cm","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["200÷35 = 5.71, so 5 full lengths can be cut: 5×35=175 cm used","200-175 = 25 cm left"]},{"id":"un15","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2022 2F Q14","q":"Iman walked for 3 hours 15 minutes. He walked a distance of 18.2 kilometres. Work out Iman's average speed for his walk. Give your answer in km/h.","answer":"5.6 km/h","level":"easy","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3 hours 15 minutes = 3.25 hours","speed = 18.2÷3.25 = 5.6 km/h"]},{"id":"un16","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 1F Q12","q":"Noah buys 3 bottles of milk at £1.45 each, 2 boxes of eggs at £2.80 each, and 2 packs of butter. Noah pays with a £20 note and receives £6.65 change. The cost of each pack of butter is the same. Work out the cost of 1 pack of butter.","answer":"£1.70","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Amount spent = 20-6.65 = 13.35","3(1.45)+2(2.80) = 4.35+5.60 = 9.95","Butter total = 13.35-9.95 = 3.40, so each pack = 3.40÷2 = 1.70"]},{"id":"un17","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 1F Q25","q":"Change a speed of 70 metres per second to a speed in kilometres per hour. Show your working clearly.","answer":"252 km/h","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["70 m/s × 3600 ÷ 1000 = 252 km/h"]},{"id":"un18","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 2F Q5","q":"The diagram shows a cup containing orange juice up to 150 ml and a jug containing orange juice up to 1.5 litres. The jug contains more orange juice than the cup. Work out how much more. State the units of your answer.","answer":"1350 ml (1.35 litres)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Jug: 1500 ml, Cup: 150 ml","1500-150 = 1350 ml"]},{"id":"un19","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 2F Q11","q":"Qaseem sells 300 tickets. 1/4 of the tickets are premium tickets costing 14 dirhams each. The remaining tickets are standard, costing 9 dirhams each. Work out the total cost of the 300 tickets.","answer":"3075 dirhams","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Premium: 300÷4=75 tickets, 75×14=1050","Standard: 225 tickets, 225×9=2025","Total = 1050+2025 = 3075"]},{"id":"un20","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2025 2F Q13","q":"Johan changes 290 euros to Hong Kong dollars. The exchange rate is 1 euro = 8.23 Hong Kong dollars. Johan gets as many 50 Hong Kong dollar notes as possible. How many 50 Hong Kong dollar notes does Johan get?","answer":"47 notes","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["290×8.23 = 2386.70 HKD","2386.70÷50 = 47.73, so 47 notes"]},{"id":"un21","topic":"units","ref":"June 2025 1F Q7","q":"The normal price of a calculator is £26.80. Amy gets 1/4 off the normal price with her student discount card. Amy buys 2 of these calculators and pays with a £50 note. How much change should Amy receive?","answer":"£9.80","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Discounted price = 26.80 × 3/4 = 20.10","2 calculators = 40.20","Change = 50-40.20 = 9.80"]},{"id":"un22","topic":"units","ref":"June 2025 1F Q12","q":"Seb went into a restaurant at 1815 and left at 2140. (a) Work out the time Seb spent in the restaurant. On Friday, the restaurant sold 120 meals, of which 48 were vegetarian. (b) What percentage of the meals sold on Friday were vegetarian meals?","answer":"(a) 3 hours 25 minutes (b) 40%","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(b) 48/120 × 100 = 40%"]},{"id":"un23","topic":"units","ref":"June 2025 2F Q7","q":"2 cupcakes and 5 doughnuts cost $4.50. 3 cupcakes cost $2.25. Work out the cost of 1 doughnut.","answer":"$0.60","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3 cupcakes = 2.25, so 1 cupcake = 0.75; 2 cupcakes = 1.50","5 doughnuts = 4.50-1.50 = 3.00, so 1 doughnut = 0.60"]},{"id":"un24","topic":"units","ref":"June 2025 2F Q9","q":"Roy has 2 litres of orange juice in a jug and some empty cups. He pours orange juice from the jug to completely fill as many cups as possible, pouring 180 millilitres into each cup. Work out how much orange juice Roy has left in the jug. Give your answer in millilitres.","answer":"20 ml","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["2000÷180 = 11.1, so 11 cups can be completely filled: 11×180=1980 ml used","2000-1980 = 20 ml left"]},{"id":"un25","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2024 1F Q6","q":"Pierre used 2358 units of water last year. Each unit cost 0.28 euros. Pierre has already paid for some of the water: he paid 42 euros each month last year. Work out how much more Pierre has to pay for the water he used last year.","answer":"156.24 euros","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Total cost = 2358×0.28 = 660.24 euros","Already paid = 42×12 = 504 euros","Remaining = 660.24-504 = 156.24 euros"]},{"id":"un26","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2024 2F Q7","q":"One weekend, Marion went on four walks of 3.5 km, 950 m, 1.8 km, and 1200 m. The same weekend, Talha walked a total of 8 kilometres, which was a greater distance than Marion walked. How much greater? Give your answer in metres.","answer":"550 m","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Marion's total = 3500+950+1800+1200 = 7450 m","Talha = 8000 m; difference = 8000-7450 = 550 m"]},{"id":"un27","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 2F Q12","q":"Shane buys a clock in Australia for 232 Australian dollars. In India, an identical clock costs 12420 Indian rupees. The exchange rate is 1 Australian dollar = 54 Indian rupees. The clock costs more in Australia than in India. Work out how much more. You must give the units of your answer.","answer":"2 Australian dollars","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["12420 rupees ÷ 54 = 230 Australian dollars","232-230 = 2 Australian dollars"]},{"id":"un28","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 2F Q19","q":"A plane takes 9 hours 36 minutes to fly from New Delhi to Perth, at an average speed of 820 km/h. Work out the total distance the plane flies.","answer":"7872 km","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["9 hours 36 minutes = 9.6 hours","distance = 820×9.6 = 7872 km"]},{"id":"un29","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 1F Q6","q":"Akbar goes to a restaurant with friends, with 1000 dirhams to spend on food. They order 2 dishes of chicken makhani at 145.50 dirhams each, 3 dishes of vegetable korma at 110 dirhams each, and as many naans as they can at 30 dirhams each. They pay with a 1000 dirham note. Work out how much change they should receive.","answer":"19 dirhams","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["2(145.50)+3(110) = 291+330 = 621","Remaining = 1000-621 = 379; naans: 379÷30 = 12.63, so 12 naans = 360","Total spent = 621+360 = 981; change = 1000-981 = 19"]},{"id":"un30","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q7","q":"(a) Write 430 pm as a time in the 24-hour clock. A bus timetable: Beetown 0845, Corthill 0950, Pilton 1036. The bus should take more time from Beetown to Corthill than from Corthill to Pilton. (b) How much more time? Give your answer in minutes.","answer":"(a) 16:30 (b) 19 minutes","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Beetown to Corthill = 65 minutes; Corthill to Pilton = 46 minutes","65-46 = 19 minutes"]},{"id":"un31","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q9","q":"3 kg of carrots and 5 kg of potatoes cost a total of 207 rand. 2 kg of the carrots cost 48 rand. Work out the cost of 1 kg of potatoes.","answer":"27 rand","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["1 kg carrots = 48÷2 = 24 rand; 3 kg carrots = 72 rand","Potatoes total = 207-72 = 135 rand; per kg = 135÷5 = 27 rand"]},{"id":"un32","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q15","q":"Yuan sells fudge: small bag 150 g for £1.80, large bag 400 g for £5. Work out which bag is better value for money. Show your working clearly.","answer":"Small bag (£0.012/g vs £0.0125/g)","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Small: 1.80÷150 = £0.012 per gram","Large: 5÷400 = £0.0125 per gram","The small bag has the lower cost per gram, so it is better value"]},{"id":"un33","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 2F Q10","q":"Adriana sells each cupcake for £2.20. Mike buys 6 of these cupcakes and pays with a £20 note. (a) Work out how much change Mike should receive. Greta sells each balloon for £0.85. Stefan has £50 to spend on balloons. (b) Work out the greatest number of balloons he can buy.","answer":"(a) £6.80 (b) 58 balloons","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 6×2.20=13.20; 20-13.20=6.80","(b) 50÷0.85 = 58.8, so 58 balloons"]},{"id":"un34","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 2F Q25","q":"Change a speed of 27 kilometres per hour to a speed in metres per second.","answer":"7.5 m/s","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["27 × 1000 ÷ 3600 = 7.5 m/s"]},{"id":"un35","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q2","q":"Luca has 5 kg of chopped tomatoes. He also has some empty tins; each tin holds 350 g of chopped tomatoes when full. Luca fills as many tins as possible. Work out the weight of the chopped tomatoes remaining. Give the units of your answer.","answer":"100 g","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["5000÷350 = 14.28, so 14 tins can be filled: 14×350=4900 g used","5000-4900 = 100 g remaining"]},{"id":"un36","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q5","q":"Parcel costs by weight band: 0<w≤1 → £6.00; 1<w≤2 → £9.02; 2<w≤5 → £15.85; 5<w≤10 → £21.90. (a) Peony sends parcels of 1.3 kg and 8 kg to two different places; work out the total cost. Gryffyn sends 3 parcels (1.5 kg, 2.8 kg, and a third) for a total cost of £33.89. (b) Work out the greatest possible weight of the third parcel.","answer":"(a) £30.92 (b) 2 kg","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) 1.3 kg → £9.02; 8 kg → £21.90; total = 30.92","(b) 1.5 kg → £9.02; 2.8 kg → £15.85; sum = 24.87; third parcel cost = 33.89-24.87 = 9.02, which is the 1<w≤2 band, so greatest possible weight = 2 kg"]},{"id":"un37","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 2F Q17","q":"Change a speed of 90 kilometres per hour to a speed in metres per second. Show your working clearly.","answer":"25 m/s","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["90 × 1000 ÷ 3600 = 25 m/s"]},{"id":"un38","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 1F Q7","q":"Sandeep has 5000 rupees to spend on flowers. He buys 6 carnations at 220 rupees each and some roses at 295 rupees each. Sandeep should receive 140 rupees in change from his 5000 rupees. Work out how many roses Sandeep buys.","answer":"12 roses","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Spent = 5000-140 = 4860","Carnations = 6×220 = 1320; Roses total = 4860-1320 = 3540","Roses = 3540÷295 = 12"]},{"id":"un39","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2F Q12","q":"Ingrid buys a bag in Sweden for 1342 Swedish Krona. The price of an identical bag in Finland is 125 euros. Using an exchange rate of 1 euro = 11 Swedish Krona, work out how much cheaper the bag is in Sweden than in Finland. You must give the units of your answer.","answer":"3 euros","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["1342÷11 = 122 euros","125-122 = 3 euros"]},{"id":"un40","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2F Q19","q":"An aeroplane travelled from New York City to Los Angeles, a distance of 3980 kilometres, in 5 hours 24 minutes. Work out the average speed of the aeroplane. Give your answer in km/h correct to the nearest whole number.","answer":"737 km/h","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["5 hours 24 minutes = 5.4 hours","3980÷5.4 = 737.04 → 737 km/h"]},{"id":"un41","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2F Q23","q":"Change a speed of 81 kilometres per hour to a speed in metres per second.","answer":"22.5 m/s","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["81 × 1000 ÷ 3600 = 22.5 m/s"]},{"id":"un42","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2022 1F Q5","q":"Angelina buys 3 packets of seeds at $2.45 each packet, 2 bags of compost at $6.20 each bag, and 4 plant pots. Each plant pot costs the same amount of money. Angelina paid a total of $34.35 for the seeds, compost and plant pots. Work out the cost of each plant pot.","answer":"$3.65","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3(2.45)+2(6.20) = 7.35+12.40 = 19.75","Pots total = 34.35-19.75 = 14.60; per pot = 14.60÷4 = 3.65"]},{"id":"un43","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2022 2FR Q10","q":"Thabisa is organising a trip to the theatre. The cost of a ticket for each adult is £11.75. The total cost of the tickets for 12 adults and 5 children is £181. Work out the cost of a ticket for each child.","answer":"£8","level":"medium","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["12 adults = 12×11.75 = 141","Remaining for 5 children = 181-141 = 40; per child = 40÷5 = 8"]},{"id":"un44","topic":"units","ref":"June 2026 1F Q21","q":"Henri competes in a race. For the first part Henri cycles 60 km at an average speed of 24 km/h. For the remaining part he runs for 1 hour 15 minutes at an average speed of 12 km/h. Work out Henri's average speed for the whole race. Give your answer in km/h. Show your working clearly.","answer":"20 km/h","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Time cycling = 60÷24 = 2.5 hours","Distance running = 12×1.25 = 15 km","Total distance = 60+15 = 75 km; total time = 2.5+1.25 = 3.75 hours","Average speed = 75÷3.75 = 20 km/h"]},{"id":"un45","topic":"units","ref":"June 2025 1F Q19","q":"Anna makes cups, each costing 6 Swiss francs to make. Each box contains 4 cups. Anna sells 80 boxes of cups for a total of 2160 Swiss francs. (a) Work out the percentage profit Anna makes. Show your working clearly. The height of each cup is 9 cm, correct to the nearest cm. (b) Write down the lower bound of the height. The weight of each cup is 120 g, correct to the nearest 10 g. (c) Write down the upper bound of the weight.","answer":"(a) 12.5% (b) 8.5 cm (c) 125 g","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Cups = 80×4=320; cost = 320×6=1920 CHF; profit = 2160-1920=240; percentage = 240/1920×100 = 12.5%"]},{"id":"un46","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 1F Q7","q":"Harold works in a factory. His normal hourly rate is £14, overtime rate is £21. Harold is paid the normal rate for 35 hours in one week. His total pay for the week is £679. Work out the number of hours of overtime he works this week.","answer":"9 hours","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Normal pay = 35×14 = 490","Overtime pay = 679-490 = 189; hours = 189÷21 = 9"]},{"id":"un47","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 1F Q23","q":"A cylinder is placed on a table, with height 21 cm. The volume of the cylinder is 1575 cm³. The force exerted by the cylinder on the table is 84 newtons. Work out the pressure on the table due to the cylinder, using pressure=force/area.","answer":"1.12 newtons/cm²","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Cross-sectional area = volume÷height = 1575÷21 = 75 cm²","pressure = 84÷75 = 1.12 N/cm²"]},{"id":"un48","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 2F Q8","q":"Bargain Crafts: crayons $4.20 per tin, offer pay for 2 get 1 free. Art's Store: pack of 5 tins for $18, offer 25% off each pack of 5. Heidi buys 30 tins from Bargain Crafts using the offer; Amir buys 30 tins from Art's Store using the offer. Work out the difference between the amount Heidi pays and the amount Amir pays.","answer":"$3","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Bargain Crafts: 30 tins in groups of 3 (pay for 2) = 10 groups, pay for 20 tins = 20×4.20 = 84","Art's Store: 18×0.75=13.50 per pack of 5; 30 tins = 6 packs = 6×13.50 = 81","Difference = 84-81 = 3"]},{"id":"un49","topic":"units","ref":"June 2024 2F Q22","q":"Change a speed of w metres per second to a speed in kilometres per hour. Give your answer in terms of w in its simplest form.","answer":"3.6w km/h","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Multiply by 3600 and divide by 1000: w×3600/1000 = 3.6w km/h"]},{"id":"un50","topic":"units","ref":"Nov 2023 2F Q13","q":"Bella buys 150 football shirts for a total cost of 1800 dollars. She gives 10% of the shirts to the local football team. Bella sells the rest of the shirts for g dollars each. She makes a total profit of 360 dollars. Work out the value of g.","answer":"g = 16","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Shirts given away = 15; shirts sold = 135","Revenue - Cost = Profit: 135g - 1800 = 360 → 135g = 2160 → g = 16"]},{"id":"un51","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 1F Q11","q":"Pablo buys some tickets to go to the theatre: 3 adult tickets at 12 euros each, and the remaining tickets for children, each costing 30% less than an adult ticket. The total amount Pablo pays for all tickets is 94.80 euros. Find the number of children's tickets Pablo buys.","answer":"7 tickets","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["3 adult tickets = 3×12 = 36 euros","Child ticket = 12×0.7 = 8.40 euros","36+8.40n = 94.80 → 8.40n = 58.80 → n = 7"]},{"id":"un52","topic":"units","ref":"June 2023 1F Q18","q":"Nanette buys 60 notebooks for a total cost of 780 dirhams. She sells 70% of the notebooks for 22 dirhams each, and the remaining notebooks for 19 dirhams each. Work out Nanette's percentage profit, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"62.3%","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["70% of 60 = 42 notebooks sold at 22: 42×22=924","Remaining 18 at 19: 18×19=342; revenue = 924+342 = 1266","Profit = 1266-780 = 486; percentage = 486/780×100 = 62.3%"]},{"id":"un53","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q6","q":"Sandeep sells 600 tickets for an event, receiving a total of $7200. 1/4 of the tickets sold are child tickets, the rest are adult tickets. The cost of an adult ticket is $13.60. Work out the cost of a child ticket.","answer":"$7.20","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Child tickets = 600÷4=150; adult tickets=450","Adult revenue = 450×13.60=6120; child revenue = 7200-6120=1080","Per child ticket = 1080÷150 = 7.20"]},{"id":"un54","topic":"units","ref":"Jan 2023 1F Q21","q":"Shane bought a car for $32000. Theresa bought a car, paying a deposit of $18000 together with 14 monthly payments of $1160. Theresa paid more than Shane. (a) Work out how much more Theresa paid as a percentage of the amount Shane paid. Kylie bought a van; after 1 year its value was $39865, having decreased by 15% during the year. (b) Work out the value of the van when Kylie bought it.","answer":"(a) 7% (b) $46900","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["(a) Theresa paid = 18000+14(1160) = 18000+16240 = 34240; difference = 34240-32000 = 2240; percentage = 2240/32000×100 = 7%","(b) 39865 is 85% of the original value: original = 39865÷0.85 = 46900"]},{"id":"un55","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 1F Q22","q":"A cylinder is placed on the ground, height 18 cm. The force exerted by the cylinder on the ground is 72 newtons. The pressure on the ground is 1.4 newtons/cm². Work out the volume of the cylinder, correct to 3 significant figures.","answer":"926 cm³","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["area = force÷pressure = 72÷1.4 = 51.43 cm²","volume = area×height = 51.43×18 = 925.7 → 926 cm³ (3 s.f.)"]},{"id":"un56","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2FR Q10","q":"It takes a machine 8 seconds to produce a bolt. Each day, the machine starts producing bolts at 0930 and produces bolts continuously every 8 seconds until it stops at 1610 the same day. Work out how many bolts the machine produces each day.","answer":"3000 bolts","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["0930 to 1610 = 6 hours 40 minutes = 400 minutes = 24000 seconds","24000÷8 = 3000 bolts"]},{"id":"un57","topic":"units","ref":"June 2022 2F Q6","q":"Special offer A: dog food normally $1.40 a tin, buy 1 get 1 half price. Special offer B: normally a pack of 6 tins for $7.20, 20% off each pack of 6. Gaspar buys 24 tins using offer A; Anna buys 24 tins using offer B. Work out the difference between the amount Gaspar pays and the amount Anna pays.","answer":"$2.16","level":"hard","qImage":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","steps":["Offer A: pairs cost 1.40+0.70=2.10; 24 tins = 12 pairs = 12×2.10 = 25.20","Offer B: 7.20×0.8=5.76 per pack of 6; 24 tins = 4 packs = 4×5.76 = 23.04","Difference = 25.20-23.04 = 2.16"]}];